# Content naming — original, not lifted

Grid Dungeon uses [game references](../docs/00-game-references.md) for **mechanics and UX**, not for **copying proper nouns** from those titles.

## Rule

When authoring **new** content (enemies, skills, items, equipment, encounter groups, Navigator kits):

- **Do not** reuse **recognizable names** from reference games (Etrian Odyssey, Mary Skelter, Wizardry, etc.) for locked `skillId` / `equipId` / `enemyId` / display names.
- **Do** reuse **genre mechanics** (FOE, AGI, strata, hub inn save, Synchro-style burst) per ADRs and system docs.
- **Tone:** match [00 — Vision § Tone](../docs/00-vision.md#tone--setting) — municipal underworks / contract crew, not medieval or sci-fi default.

## Allowed vs not

| OK | Avoid (examples) |
|----|------------------|
| `patch_kit`, `stim_draft`, `trauma_kit`, `foe_alley_stalker` | `medica`, `amrita`, `nectar`, `union_strike` |
| `protocol_strike`, `guild_handler` | EO Union skill names, EO Navigator names |
| Generic combat verbs: Guard, Attack, Flee | — |
| **FOE** as a system term (documented ADR) | Copying EO enemy *display* names verbatim |

Renames already locked: [ADR 020](../decisions/020-team-burst-naming.md) (Union → Synchro). Consumables: [character progression § Consumables](../docs/02-systems/character-progression.md#consumables-starter).

## When editing existing locked IDs

- **Do not rename** locked IDs in [05-class-design.md](../docs/05-class-design.md#content-ids-locked) without an explicit ticket — saves and game assets depend on them.
- New rows in content tables (e.g. [enemy-roster.md](../docs/03-content/enemy-roster.md)) must follow this rule before merge.

## PR / agent self-check

Before proposing new content IDs, ask: *Would an EO player read this name as a direct lift?* If yes, pick an in-world name that fits the tone brief.

## Game repo

Same rule applies when adding `Assets/Content/**` ScriptableObjects — IDs must match design-docs locked tables; display names follow the same originality rule.
